The 2024 email open rate was about 29.29%. That is total unique opens divided by total emails sent: 1,545,509 / 5,276,594.

It covers the 53 weeks whose Monday falls in 2024, from 2024-01-01 through 2024-12-30, across all 20 regions. Unique opens are counted per email, so this is a unique-open rate.

{"answer": 29.29, "refused": false}

I can't calculate a churn rate for 2025 from this data, so I'm not giving a number.

The tables have no customer, subscription, renewal or cancellation data. The only sales-outcome data is `crm_opportunities`, whose stages are Open, Closed Won and Closed Lost. Closed Lost means a lost sales deal. It doesn't mean an existing customer left. To compute churn I would also need a definition (logo or revenue churn) and a record of which customers were active at the start of 2025 and which cancelled.

